  "derivation": "For k nonzero tasks all oriented favourably, only their all-positive sign pattern reaches the maximum; zero tasks multiply both numerator and denominator. Hence minimum attainable one-sided p=2**(-k), with ties included. Any unfavourable signs only weaken this bound.",
  "interpretation": [
    "Six heldout tasks/category cannot support a20-hypothesis exact signflip/Holm family, even if every task difference favours the intended direction.",
    "Freezing only one discovery-selected pair and its two directions before independent heldout data makes a2-hypothesis family coherent, but with six tasks both contrasts still have coarse resolution and substantial ties can prevent rejection.",
    "More initial states can improve estimates and reduce zero task differences; they do not turn repeated cases into additional task clusters.",
    "If the next branch retains a six-task prompt-disjoint holdout, define a scientifically justified primary family before holdout, or enlarge the task pool or report the panel as exploratory.",
    "Keeping all12tasks/category with fresh initial states is another design option when task-disjoint generalization is not the scientific claim.",
    "Do not change the current432/360study, weaken its criterion, select the family from heldout results, or treat non-significance as absence of complementarity."
  ],
